INSERT INTO characters (slug,name,team,creator,owner_id,tags,appears_in,data,url_slug,status,updated_at,created_at) VALUES
('bludbaythe','Bludbaythe','demon','legitch',NULL,'','SCP Fragmented Veil','{"slug":"bludbaythe","name":"Bludbaythe","team":"demon","ability":"All players know you are in play & what your ability is. For each minion, the Storyteller will give a public hint at any time. [Minions can be from any set]","creator":"legitch","appearsIn":"SCP Fragmented Veil","lede":"SCP-354 is a pool of a blood-like substance that brings in waves of monsters and terrors from other worlds to do battle against mankind.","summaryBullets":["The Bludbaythe can bring in any Minion from anywhere. All players know what possible sets ''anywhere'' entails.","However, the Bludbaythe outs their existence to all players, making them alert and ready for any possible Minion shenanigans.","Additionally, all Minions will have a hint about them brought forth by the Storyteller over the course of the game."],"howToRun":["While setting up the game, replace the Minion character tokens with Minion tokens from any set you possess. Decide what special ability the Bludbaythe has.","While preparing the first night, put the Bludbaythe''s **HINT** reminder token by each Minion character token.","Immediately after dawn on the first day, declare that the Bludbaythe is in play, inform the group of the special ability the Bludbaythe has this game, and what possible sets Minions can come from.","During the game, treat that player as if they had that ability, waking them when needed, prompting them to choose players when needed, or whatever else is appropriate. Use the Bludbaythe''s **?** reminders if you need to.","At any time {{i|(even at night)}}, if you decide too, remove a **HINT** reminder from a Minion, and declare a cryptic hint regarding that Minion."],"examples":["One of the in-play Minions is a Baron. At dawn, the Storyteller believes that evil is already winning substantially via a lucky kill on the barber, so the Storyteller gives the hint (in the form of a rhyme): {{i|\"From cobble brings smoke, in the central venture, the wheel turns for this arrow to the clouds, indefinite pleasure.\"}}"],"tips":["The Bludbaythe is an incredibly sophisticated and enigmatic character, and is recommended for both experienced players and Storytellers.","It''s generally a good idea for all Minions brought in by the Bludbaythe to be quiet minions which don''t announce their presence, and to also disallow Minions which can suddenly end games by some sort of condition failing to be met.","There is no official standard for what types of texts the hints are. They may be cryptic riddles that use word play, or direct factual information - both examples can do a good job to facilitate discussion amongst the circle of people. It''s the Storyteller''s job to create an engaging game for all players using this lack of restriction to their advantage.","The Bludbaythe''s special ability may be as simple or as complex as you want to fit the gameplay and the Minions you added. Some good examples of special abilities include: \"Each night*, choose a player: they die. You die if **{{i|(& only if)}}** **all other Minions are dead.\"**, or also: **\"After day 5, evil wins. If a good player is executed, this comes closer by a day.\"** It''s recommended you make abilities that don''t make the Bludbaythe wake on the first night to prevent confusion with the first night order."],"iconBy":"le_nuberto","jinxes":[{"name":"Alchemist","align":"good","text":"The Alchemist cannot have off-script Minion abilities.","id":"alchemist"},{"name":"Dreamer","align":"good","text":"The Dreamer visits the Storyteller during each day to choose a player instead of waking up each night, and instead of learning 1 evil character at most, they learn up to 3 Minions and/or the Bludbaythe, alongside the 1 good character.","id":"dreamer"},{"name":"Engineer","align":"good","text":"Only 1 jinxed character can be in play.","id":"engineer"},{"name":"Hatter","align":"good","text":"The Hatter''s ability can only transform others into on-script Minions.","id":"hatter"},{"name":"Investigator","align":"good","text":"The Investigator might learn 2 to 4 particular Minions their target could be, instead of just 1.","id":"investigator"},{"name":"Juggler","align":"good","text":"For each Juggler guess not used on their first day (up to 3), the Juggler may publicly guess a Minion that is in-play the day a hint is given, for each hint, and learn how many they got correct that night.","id":"juggler"},{"name":"King","align":"good","text":"The King cannot learn evil characters. Each night, the King (after learning an alive character if valid) chooses a hint you gave & a player: if that player is the one the hint referred too, they learn this, it cannot misregister or be false.","id":"king"},{"name":"Pit-Hag","align":"evil","text":"The Pit-Hag cannot create off-script Minions.","id":"pithag"},{"name":"Plague Doctor","align":"good","text":"If the Plague Doctor dies, a Minion (living or dead) learns that they''ll keep their ability when dead.","id":"plaguedoctor"},{"name":"Sauelsuesor","align":"good","text":"The Sauelsuesor only learns if they nominated a Minion, and doesn''t know which Minion they are,","slug":"sauelsuesor"},{"name":"Cobbler","align":"good","text":"The Cobbler might learn 2 to 4 Minions that is in-play or not in-play with the good character, instead of just 1 evil character.","id":"cobbler_hblreleased"},{"name":"Porcher","align":"good","text":"If the Bludbaythe swaps to a different ability, hints will still be given out as appropiate.","id":"porcher_hblreleased"},{"name":"Wig Snatcher","align":"good","text":"The Wig Snatcher cannot become a Minion through their ability, but learns if they wouldve.","id":"wigsnatcher_hblreleased"},{"name":"Archivist","align":"good","text":"The Archivist''s questions will instead pertain a publicly given hint of the Archivist''s choice that corresponds to the associated Minion.","id":"archivist_the_bootleggers_anthology"},{"name":"Falconer","align":"evil","text":"The Falconer can choose to not use their ability on the 1st night, inexchange for being able to use it every night proceding a day where a hint was given out, only being able to select 3 Minions at the same time.","id":"falconer_the_bootleggers_anthology"},{"name":"Local Hero","align":"good","text":"The Local Hero might learn 2 to 4 opposing Minions, instead of just 1, but they''re still referring to the same player.","id":"localhero_the_bootleggers_anthology"},{"name":"Penitent","align":"good","text":"If the Bludbaythe exchanges their ability, hints will still be given out as appropiate.","id":"penitent_the_bootleggers_anthology"},{"name":"Skeptic","align":"good","text":"If the Skeptic starts in-play, players are not announced that the Bludbaythe is in-play, and their special ability is \"Each night*, choose a player: they die.\".","id":"skeptic"},{"name":"Yinyang Diviner","align":"good","text":"The Yin-Yang Diviner might instead learns 4 to 8 Minions.","id":"yinyang_diviner_festival_of_lanterns"},{"name":"Aesthete","align":"good","text":"The Aesthete cannot learn in-play Minions.","id":"aesthete_2tfafullcharacterlist"},{"name":"Boxer","align":"good","text":"The Boxer does not learn the Minion''s character, only that they were chosen.","id":"boxer_2tfafullcharacterlist"},{"name":"Disciple","align":"evil","text":"The Disciple might learn 2 to 4 opposing Minions, instead of just 1.","id":"disciple_darkartists_stuff"}],"customBoxes":[{"title":"In the almanac JSON","content":"**First night:** Announce ''the Bludbaythe is in play'', inform the group of the special ability the Bludbaythe has this game, and what possible sets Minions can come from. It is recommended you change this announcement to make it more thematic whilst keeping it''s contents.\n**Other nights:** If the Bludbaythe''s special ability causes them to wake tonight: Wake the Bludbaythe and run their ability.\n**Reminders:** Hint, Hint, Hint, Hint, Dead, ?, ?, ?"}],"firstNight":73.354,"otherNight":51.354,"reminders":["Hint","Hint","Hint","Dead","?","?","?"],"setup":true,"firstNightReminder":"Announce ''SCP-354 is in play'', inform the group of the special ability SCP-354 has this game, and what possible sets Minions can come from. It is recommended you change this announcement to make it more thematic whilst keeping it''s contents.","otherNightReminder":"If SCP-354''s special ability causes them to wake tonight: Wake SCP-354 and run their ability.","art":"art/bludbaythe.png","jsonId":"bludbaythe_scp_fragmented_veil","curata":false}','scp-fragmented-veil/bludbaythe','published',datetime('now'),datetime('now')),
('pyrrite','Pyrrite','demon','legitch',NULL,'','SCP Fragmented Veil','{"slug":"pyrrite","name":"Pyrrite","team":"demon","ability":"Each night after the 2nd, choose half of all living players (max 6): they die.","creator":"legitch","appearsIn":"SCP Fragmented Veil","lede":"SCP-457 is a constantly burning humanoid with a primitive instinct to burn everything to ashes.","summaryBullets":["On the 3rd night and beyond, the Pyrrite begins the burndown - they choose half of all living players {{i|(rounded up)}} to die.","The Pyrrite directly kills players in the order chosen and can only choose to kill living players.","The Pyrrite is capped at killing at most 6 players through their ability per night. They cannot kill more than that."],"howToRun":["Each night except the first and second, wake the Pyrrite. They point to half of all living players {{i|(rounded up, maximum of 6)}}, one at a time {{i|(if the player is unsure how many players they should be pointing to, you may also show the finger symbol for that number to help them out)}}. Put the Pyrrite to sleep. In the order chosen, each chosen player {{i|dies}} - mark them with **DEAD** reminders."],"iconBy":"le_nuberto","jinxes":[{"name":"Goon","align":"good","text":"If the Pyrrite is drunkened by the Goon, they are immune to it the next night.","id":"goon"},{"name":"Neglected","align":"good","text":"If the Pyrrite is drunkened by the Neglected, they are immune to it the next night.","slug":"neglected"}],"customBoxes":[{"title":"Alternative JSON & How to Run (Older)","content":"If you want to use the older version of the Pyrrite, where it had a Recluse-like effect before starting the burndown of death a day later, use this JSON. It is much more complex than the current version, and may be more unwarranted due to that alone.\n\nWhen preparing the first night, put the Pyrrite’s **NIGHT 1** reminder by the Pyrrite. When preparing the second night, put the Pyrrite’s **NIGHT 2** reminder by the Pyrrite. When preparing the third night, put the Pyrrite’s **NIGHT 3** reminder by the Pyrrite. When preparing the fourth night, put the Pyrrite''s **NIGHT 4** reminder by the Pyrrite.\n\nEach night, wake the Pyrrite.\n\nIf they are not marked with the **NIGHT 4** reminder, they point at any player. The chosen player might migregister by evil - put the **RECLUSIVE** reminder token by the chosen player''s character token. Put the Pyrrite to sleep. Each time a player marked **RECLUSIVE** is targeted by an ability that detects or affects evil characters, choose which character and alignment that player registers as. Do whatever is appropriate, such as showing an evil character token, nodding, giving finger signals, or allowing an ability to work that would normally only affect evil, Minion, or Demon players.\n\nIf they are marked with the **NIGHT 4** reminder, they point to half of all living players (rounded up), one at a time {{i|(if the player is unsure how many players they should be pointing to, you may also show the finger symbol for that number to help them out)}}. Put the Pyrrite to sleep. In the order chosen, each chosen player dies - mark them with **DEAD** reminders.\n\n**Pyrrite █~** (Demon)\nEach night after the 3rd, choose half of all living players: they die. Each night before that, choose a player: they might register as evil & an evil character.\n\n**First night:** The Pyrrite points to a player. That player might register as evil and a Minion or Demon.\n**Other nights:** If it is the 2nd or 3rd night, the Pyrrite points to a player. That player might register as evil and a Minion or Demon. If it is the 4th night or beyond, the Pyrrite points to half of all living players. Those players die.\n**Reminders:** Night 1, Night 2, Night 3, Night 4+, Reclusive, Reclusive, Reclusive, Dead, Dead, Dead, Dead, Dead, Dead, Dead\n**Credit:** Ability: @legitch. Image: @le_nuberto\n\n**Jinxes:**\nGoon: If the Pyrrite is drunkened by the Goon, they are immune to it the next night.\nOgre: If a misregistered player registers as evil to the Ogre, the Ogre learns that they are evil.\nNeglected: If the Pyrrite is drunkened by the Neglected, they are immune to it the next night."}],"firstNight":0,"otherNight":47.457,"reminders":["Dead","Dead","Dead","Dead","Dead","Dead"],"setup":false,"otherNightReminder":"If it is the 3rd night or beyond, the Pyrrite points to half of all living players (maximum of 6). Those players die.","art":"art/pyrrite.png","jsonId":"pyrrite_scp_fragmented_veil","curata":false}','scp-fragmented-veil/pyrrite','published',datetime('now'),datetime('now')),
('peredatore','Peredatore','demon','legitch',NULL,'','SCP Fragmented Veil','{"slug":"peredatore","name":"Peredatore","team":"demon","ability":"Each night*, choose a player: they die. With 3+ dead, you can only choose their neighbors, but evils you kill only register as it.","creator":"legitch","appearsIn":"SCP Fragmented Veil","lede":"The Peredatore (SCP-575) is a shapeless darkness with predator instincts. It solidifies darkness as a whole to envelope and consume all.","summaryBullets":["The Peredatore has little agency over their kills, having a limited choice on who they can choose dies once there are 3 or more dead players.","Any players that neighbour another dead player can be a potential victim to the Peredatore, whether it was the Peredatore''s first few victim(s), a player that died by execution during the day, or another player''s ability.","Whilst the Peredatore is restricted to the neighbours of the dead, kills made during this by the Peredatore on evil players don''t actually kill them.","Those falsely registering as dead will remain alive, but appear to be dead for intents and purposes, even if they of the Peredatore changes character, similar to the Zombuul.","Evil players killed by other methods, whether alive or falsely dead, won''t survive or falsely register as dead to the public."],"howToRun":["Each night except the first, wake the Peredatore. If there are 3 or more dead players, they must point to anyone neighbouring a dead player, otherwise, they point at any player. That player {{i|dies}} - mark them with the **DEAD** reminder, or if they are a living evil player, there are 3 or more dead players, instead mark them with the **FALSELY DEAD** reminder - they remain alive, and you''ll declare that they died, but do not add a shroud to them. From now on, register them as dead."],"iconBy":"le_nuberto","firstNight":0,"otherNight":37.575,"reminders":["Falsely dead","Falsely dead","Falsely dead","Falsely dead","Falsely dead","Dead"],"setup":false,"otherNightReminder":"If there is at least 3 dead players: The Peredatore points to a player neighbouring another dead player. Otherwise: The Peredatore points to a player. That player dies.","art":"art/peredatore.png","jsonId":"peredatore_scp_fragmented_veil","curata":false}','scp-fragmented-veil/peredatore','published',datetime('now'),datetime('now'));
